<!-- ═════════════ SECTION 2 · CHALLENGE & BUILD ═════════════ -->
<section id="build" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="num">02</span>
      <span class="kicker">Why this site · What was built</span>
      <h2>The challenge &amp; the custom build</h2>
      <p>GIBS is a Chittagong institute offering diploma to postgraduate courses with British awarding bodies such as Pearson Edexcel and AIA. Its old website dated from 2013, and its online learning ran separately from the site.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="split">
      <div class="problems rv">
        <h3>Problems to solve</h3>
        <ol><li><span class="pi">01</span><div><b>A dated legacy site</b><p>Content from 2013 sat in an old CMS. It was hard to update and didn&#x27;t reflect an internationally affiliated institute.</p></div></li><li><span class="pi">02</span><div><b>Programmes not visible</b><p>Diplomas, top-up degrees, postgraduate and language courses had no strong visual showcase.</p></div></li><li><span class="pi">03</span><div><b>Separate e-learning</b><p>Online degrees and certificate programmes had no clear entry point from the main website.</p></div></li><li><span class="pi">04</span><div><b>Forgotten history</b><p>Years of events (ICPSD 2014, the Chittagong University visit 2017, a Pearson visit, graduations) had nowhere to live online.</p></div></li></ol>
      </div>
      <div class="stack rv">
        <div class="stack-stage" id="stackStage"><div class="scard" data-title="Branded Moodle LMS (/lms)" data-desc="A Moodle LMS on the institute&#x27;s own domain, branded in GIBS green, for online degrees, certificate programmes and self-paced courses."><span class="cap">01 · Feature</span><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Branded Moodle LMS (/lms)"></div><div class="scard" data-title="Leadership &amp; Vision" data-desc="Messages from the MD and Chairman with custom shape masks, credentials and profile links for academic credibility."><span class="cap">02 · Feature</span><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Leadership &amp; Vision"></div><div class="scard" data-title="Media Archive" data-desc="Campus and Pearson Edexcel visit galleries, 5 event collections and a 4-video YouTube gallery, all with a lightbox."><span class="cap">03 · Feature</span><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Media Archive"></div></div>
        <div class="stack-info">
          <div><h4 id="stTitle"></h4><p id="stDesc"></p></div>
          <div class="dots" id="stDots"><button aria-label="Feature 1">1</button><button aria-label="Feature 2">2</button><button aria-label="Feature 3">3</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="builds-title rv">Special features &amp; customisation</h3>
    <div class="build-grid"><article class="bcard rv"><span class="n">01</span><h4>Legacy migration</h4><p>Content from 2013 was moved into modern Elementor layouts: About, Why Study, Admission, Affiliations, Fees, Financial Aid, Career Advice, FAQ and more (25+ pages).</p><span class="t">Content migration</span></article><article class="bcard rv"><span class="n">02</span><h4>13-slide course hero</h4><p>A layered Slider Revolution hero for IoT, Cyber Security, Software Engineering and other programmes, with motion.</p><span class="t">Slider Revolution 6</span></article><article class="bcard rv"><span class="n">03</span><h4>Moodle LMS integration</h4><p>A Moodle LMS at /lms, themed to match the brand, with a green “LMS” button in the main navigation.</p><span class="t">Moodle · Theming</span></article><article class="bcard rv"><span class="n">04</span><h4>Media archive</h4><p>A 16-photo Pearson visit gallery, campus galleries, 5 event galleries (ICPSD, CU visit, graduation…) and 4 embedded videos.</p><span class="t">Elementor galleries</span></article><article class="bcard rv"><span class="n">05</span><h4>Download centre</h4><p>Application form and admission-procedure PDFs sit in a dedicated Download menu, so offline applicants are covered too.</p><span class="t">Dropdown navigation</span></article><article class="bcard rv"><span class="n">06</span><h4>Reusable blueprint</h4><p>The same WordPress + Moodle pattern was reused across the group: BCET LMS, KIGS LMS and the Digital Library.</p><span class="t">Scalable architecture</span></article></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═════════════ SECTION 3 · IMPACT ═════════════ -->
<section id="impact" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="num">03</span>
      <span class="kicker">Results · Problems solved</span>
      <h2>The impact</h2>
      <p>The institute now has one digital campus that reflects its international standing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stats"><div class="stat rv"><b><span data-to="13">0</span><i></i></b><span>Animated hero slides</span></div><div class="stat rv"><b><span data-to="25">0</span><i>+</i></b><span>Pages migrated &amp; rebuilt</span></div><div class="stat rv"><b><span data-to="5">0</span><i></i></b><span>Event galleries + 4 videos</span></div><div class="stat rv"><b><span data-to="1">0</span><i></i></b><span>Integrated Moodle LMS</span></div></div>
    <div class="impact-split">
      <div class="outcomes"><div class="oc rv"><b>Looks like what it is</b><p>A modern, affiliation-first website that matches a British-accredited institute.</p></div><div class="oc rv"><b>Apply offline or learn online</b><p>PDF applications and the Moodle LMS are both one click from the main menu.</p></div><div class="oc rv"><b>History becomes proof</b><p>A decade of conferences, visits and graduations now builds credibility instead of being lost.</p></div><div class="oc rv"><b>A template for the group</b><p>The architecture was reused for sister institutions&#x27; LMS and library portals.</p></div></div>
      <div class="ring-wrap rv" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ring3d"><div class="rc">WordPress</div><div class="rc">Astra</div><div class="rc">Elementor Pro</div><div class="rc">Slider Revolution</div><div class="rc">WPForms</div><div class="rc">Moodle LMS</div><div class="rc">YouTube Embeds</div><div class="rc">Lightbox Galleries</div></div>
        <div class="ring-core">Built on<br>WordPress</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="closing rv">
      <p>From a 2013-era website to a <b>connected digital campus</b>: website, archive and Moodle LMS under one brand.</p>
